## Why This Is Asked

This question assesses practical knowledge of testing streaming systems, with emphasis on edge-case window behavior, fault tolerance, and end-to-end accuracy—skills essential for building production-grade data platforms.

## Key Concepts

- Windowing semantics and latency boundaries
- Idempotent and deduplicated alerting
- End-to-end streaming integration patterns
- Backpressure handling and burst tolerance
- Observability and feature drift detection

## Code Example

```javascript
// Unit test for window aggregation correctness
async function testWindowAggregation() {
  const windowService = new WindowingService({
    windowSizeMs: 5000,
    slideIntervalMs: 1000
  });

  // Simulate late-arriving events within watermark tolerance
  await windowService.processEvents([
    { timestamp: 1000, value: 10 },
    { timestamp: 2000, value: 20 },
    { timestamp: 5500, value: 30 } // Late event within tolerance
  ]);

  const result = await windowService.getWindowResult();
  expect(result.sum).toBe(60);
  expect(result.count).toBe(3);
}

// Integration test for alert deduplication
async function testAlertDeduplication() {
  const alertService = new AlertService();

  // Simulate duplicate events from Kafka retry
  for (let i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
    await alertService.process({
      eventId: 'evt-123',
      anomalyScore: 0.95,
      timestamp: Date.now()
    });
  }

  const alerts = await alertService.getEmittedAlerts();
  expect(alerts.length).toBe(1); // Only one alert emitted
}
```

